    {
      "beat_id": "B02",
      "act": "BODY",
      "narration_text": "The first was a security bug: an admin could get around the rule that you can't change your own account, by writing their I D in a different format. I fixed it, and tested eight formats. The second was an account takeover risk: change someone's email, then reset their password. Now P M and admin emails can only be changed by the owner, and other changes must be confirmed from the member's current email.",
      "voice": "am_michael",
      "engine": "kokoro",
      "estimated_duration_s": 16,
      "shot": {
        "type": "REMOTION",
        "source": "remotion",
